#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:1
msgid "Feature Name: `abi_custom`"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:2
msgid "Start Date: 2026-07-01"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:3
msgid ""
"RFC PR: [rust-lang/rfcs#3980](https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3980)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:4
msgid ""
"Rust Issue: [rust-lang/rust#140829](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"issues/140829)"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:6
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:9
msgid ""
"An `extern \"custom\" fn` is a function with a custom ABI that is unknown to "
"Rust. Often these are low-level functions that pass arguments in different "
"registers than any standard calling convention, so using `extern \"custom\"` "
"helps rustc block you from using a function in a place where rustc would "
"need to understand that calling convention."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:13
msgid ""
"/// # SAFETY\n"
"///\n"
"/// - Expects the dividend and the divisor in r0 and r1.\n"
"/// - Returns the quotient in r0 and the remainder in r1.\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:18 src/3980-extern-custom.md:31
msgid "\"custom\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:20
msgid "\"push {{lr}}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:21
msgid "\"sub sp, sp, #4\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:22
msgid "\"mov r2, sp\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:23
msgid "\"bl {trampoline}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:24
msgid "\"ldr r1, [sp]\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:25
msgid "\"add sp, sp, #4\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:26
msgid "\"pop {{pc}}\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:36
msgid "History"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:38
msgid "Proposal: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/140566"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:39
msgid "Tracking issue: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/140829"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:40
msgid "Implementation: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/140770"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:41
msgid ""
"Restrictions on function pointer types: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/"
"pull/159780"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:42
msgid "Stabilization PR: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/158504"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:44
msgid "Motivation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:47
msgid ""
"In some low-level scenarios we must define naked functions with a custom "
"ABI. This comes up in `rust-lang/compiler-builtins` (e.g. for "
"`__rust_probestack` and `__aeabi_uidivmod`), and also in systems programming "
"(e.g. when defining `__fentry__`, a symbol used the mcount mechanism)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:49
msgid ""
"The current solution is often to use `extern \"C\"`, but that is misleading: "
"the function does not use the C calling convention, and calling it as if it "
"were is almost certainly causing UB."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:51
msgid "Guide-level explanation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:54
msgid ""
"Because Rust doesn't know what calling convention to use, an `extern "
"\"custom\"` function can only be called via inline assembly or FFI."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:56
msgid ""
"```\n"
"error: functions with the \"custom\" ABI cannot be called\n"
" --> <source>:5:5\n"
"  |\n"
"5 |     bar();\n"
"  |     ^^^^^\n"
"  |\n"
"note: an `extern \"custom\"` function can only be called using inline "
"assembly\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:66
msgid "An `extern \"custom\"` function definition must be a naked function:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:68
msgid ""
"```\n"
"error: items with the \"custom\" ABI can only be declared externally or "
"defined via naked functions\n"
"  --> <source>:10:1\n"
"   |\n"
"10 | unsafe extern \"custom\" fn bar() {\n"
"   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n"
"   |\n"
"help: convert this to an `#[unsafe(naked)]` function\n"
"   |\n"
"10 + #[unsafe(naked)]\n"
"11 | unsafe extern \"custom\" fn bar() {\n"
"   |\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:82
msgid ""
"An `extern \"custom\"` function definition must be unsafe. The intent here "
"is that a safety comment is written on how this function may be called."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:84
msgid ""
"```\n"
"error: functions with the \"custom\" ABI must be unsafe\n"
"  --> <source>:10:1\n"
"   |\n"
"10 | extern \"custom\" fn bar() {\n"
"   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n"
"   |\n"
"help: add the `unsafe` keyword to this definition\n"
"   |\n"
"10 | unsafe extern \"custom\" fn bar() {\n"
"   | ++++++\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:97
msgid "In an `extern \"custom\"` block, functions cannot be marked as `safe`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:99
msgid ""
"```\n"
"error: foreign functions with the \"custom\" ABI cannot be safe\n"
"  --> <source>:16:5\n"
"   |\n"
"16 |     safe fn foobar();\n"
"   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n"
"   |\n"
"help: remove the `safe` keyword from this definition\n"
"   |\n"
"16 -     safe fn foobar();\n"
"16 +     fn foobar();\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:112
msgid ""
"An `extern \"custom\"` function cannot have any arguments or a return type:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:114
msgid ""
"```\n"
"error: invalid signature for `extern \"custom\"` function\n"
" --> <source>:6:31\n"
"  |\n"
"6 | unsafe extern \"custom\" fn foo(a: i32) -> i32 {\n"
"  |                               ^^^^^^     ^^^\n"
"  |\n"
"  = note: functions with the \"custom\" ABI cannot have any parameters or "
"return type\n"
"help: remove the parameters and return type\n"
"  |\n"
"6 - unsafe extern \"custom\" fn foo(a: i32) -> i32 {\n"
"6 + unsafe extern \"custom\" fn foo() {\n"
"  |\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:129
msgid ""
"We also error on missing `unsafe` or presence of argument and return types "
"in `extern` blocks and function pointer types."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:131
msgid ""
"```\n"
"error: invalid signature for `extern \"custom\"` function\n"
"  --> $DIR/bad-custom.rs:13:40\n"
"   |\n"
"LL | type MustbeUnsafe = extern \"custom\" fn(i64) -> i64;\n"
"   |                                        ^^^     ^^^\n"
"   |\n"
"   = note: functions with the \"custom\" ABI cannot have any parameters or "
"return type\n"
"help: remove the parameters and return type\n"
"   |\n"
"LL - type MustbeUnsafe = extern \"custom\" fn(i64) -> i64;\n"
"LL + type MustbeUnsafe = extern \"custom\" fn();\n"
"   |\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:146
msgid "Reference-level explanation"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:149
msgid "See https://github.com/rust-lang/reference/pull/2300."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:151
msgid "Drawbacks"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:154
msgid "No specific drawback."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:156
msgid "Rationale and alternatives"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:159
msgid "https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/140566"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:161
msgid ""
"The name has already been debated. The name `unknown` has been mentioned, "
"but to write the implementation you really do need to know the ABI. It is "
"custom in the sense that rustc does not know about it, but the author "
"definitely does."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:163
msgid ""
"Arguments and return types are forbidden because they are not consumed in "
"any way. The compiler has no way of validating them against the function "
"body, similar to other naked functions, but the functions can never be "
"invoked directly so they serve no purpose when calling. The intent is that "
"correct parameter passing and returning will be covered in documentation."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:165
msgid "Prior art"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:168
msgid "https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/140566#issuecomment-2846205457"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:170
msgid ""
"We do have some other calling conventions that cannot be called using Rust's "
"function calling syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:172
msgid "extern \"\\*\\-interrupt\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:173
msgid "extern \"gpu-kernel\""
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:175
msgid ""
"Those however do have a known ABI, it's just that semantically it does not "
"make sense to call them from a Rust program."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:177
msgid "Unresolved questions"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:180
msgid "None currently."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:182
msgid "Future possibilities"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:185
msgid "Support `Never` as a return type"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:187
msgid "A return type of `-> !` indicates that the function diverges."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:189
msgid ""
"That a function diverges is useful to know, and relevant for the very low-"
"level use cases for `extern \"custom\"`. However, like arbirary argument and "
"return types (see below), the type is never actually validated, and the "
"signature might go out of sync with the implementation."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:193
msgid ""
"So far, no actual use of `-> !` has come up, so we leave it as a future "
"possibility."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:195
msgid "Support argument and return types"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:197
msgid "Argument and return types are not validated by the compiler whatsoever:"
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:199
msgid ""
"Like any other `#[naked]` function, argument/return types are not validated "
"against the body."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:200
msgid ""
"Argument/return types are not validated at the call site (because inline "
"assembly is used)."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:202
msgid ""
"For those reasons, argument and return types are omitted in the current RFC."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:204
msgid ""
"The only place where the argument/return types would be checked is when an "
"`extern \"custom\"` function pointer is unified again another function "
"pointer type. A newtype wrapper can be used to differentiate different "
"`extern \"custom\"` function pointers that carry a particular semantic "
"meaning."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:208
msgid ""
"However, the point has been raised that the argument and return types can "
"serve as documentation. On the other hand, the signature can be misleading: "
"the whole point of `extern \"custom\"` is that no known ABI is followed."
msgstr ""

#: src/3980-extern-custom.md:211
msgid ""
"In summary, we leave space for argument and return types to be supported in "
"the future when a compelling use case presents itself."
msgstr ""
